--------------- Adventurer's Guide to Weapons and Armor --------------------
 
I think the part on Bows still needs a little work, but here's a quick list
of useful information about all the standard (non-artifact) weapons and armors.
There's also a short bit about how Strength and Dexterity affect your chances
to hit and your damage (for non-missile weapons).
 
--Robert DeLoura
deloura@noaapmel.gov
 
 
	 The Adventurer's Guide to Standard Weapons and Armor
			  by Robert DeLoura
			 deloura@noaapmel.gov
 
 
Your STR and DEX affect your chances to hit and your amount of damage in
combat.
 
                       Stat          To-Hit          Damage
           -------------------------------------------------
                     STR < 6           -2              -1
                6 <= STR < 8           -1            normal
                8 <= STR < 16        normal          normal
                     STR = 16        normal            +1
                     STR = 17          +1              +1
                     STR = 18          +1              +2
            18/01 <= STR < 18/50       +1              +3
            18/51 <= STR < 18/75       +2              +3
	    18/75 <= STR < 18/90       +2              +4
            18/90 <= STR < 18/**       +2              +5
                     STR = 18/**       +3              +6
 
                     DEX < 4           -3            normal
                4 <= DEX < 6           -2            normal
                6 <= DEX < 8           -1            normal
                8 <= DEX < 14        normal          normal
                     DEX = 15          +1            normal
                     DEX = 16          +2            normal
                     DEX = 17          +3            normal
                     DEX = 18          +4            normal
                       ....           ....            ....
 
The DEX part of the table just continues on, with the bonus To-Hit being
(DEX - 14), and no damage bonus ever being given for DEX.
 
A plus on a weapon, pickaxe, or unicorn horn adds to its chance of hitting.
Blessed weapons are +2 To-Hit against Demons and Undead.
Spears and Javelins are +2 to-hit against Xorn, Dragons, Nagas, and Giants.
 
A plus on a weapon, pickaxe, or unicorn horn also adds to its damage.
Weapons are -1 to damage for each time they've rusted.
Cream Pies do NO damage.
Leather weapons (bullwhips) do NO damage against thick-skinned creatures.
  [Small Mimics, Large Mimics, Giant Mimics, Mumaks, Titanotheres,
  Baluchitheriums, Baby Dragons, Dragons, Earth Elementals, Naga Hatchlings,
  Nagas, Xorn, Skeletons, Wood Golems, Clay Golems, Stone Golems, Iron
  Golems, Horned Devils, Barbed Devils, Crocodiles, the Chromatic Dragon*
  (Caveman's Quest Nemesis), and Ixoth* (Knight's Quest Nemesis).]
Axes and Battle Axes do +d4 (+2.5 avg) damage against wooden creatures.
  [Wood Golems.]
Blessed weapons do +d4 (+2.5 avg) damage against Undead and Demons.
  [UNDEAD are:  Vampire Bats, all Liches, all Mummies, all Vampires including
  Vlad the Impaler, Barrow Wights, Wraiths, Nazgul, all Zombies, Skeletons,
  Ghosts, and Shades.]
  [DEMONS are:  Water Demons, Erinyes, Horned Devils, Succubi, Incubi, Barbed
  Devils, Mariliths, Vrocks, Hezrou, Bone Devils, Ice Devils, Nalfeshnee,
  Pit Fiends, Balrogs, the Minion of Huhetol* (Archeologist's Quest Nemesis),
  and Nalzok* (Priest's Quest Nemesis).  Also, the following demon lords and
  princes:  Demogorgon, Juiblex, Yeenoghu, Orcus, Geryon, Dispater, Baalzebub,
  Asmodeus.]
  [AD&D players might think the following creatures are demons, but for the
  purposes of Nethack, they are not:  Manes, Homunculi, Imps, Lemures,
  Quasits, and Tengu.]
Silver weapons do +d20 (+10.5 avg) damage against silver-hating creatures.
  [All Were-creatures, all Demons, Shades, any monster represented by a
  'V' (all Vampire types including Vlad), and any monster represented by
  an 'i' EXCEPT for Tengus.]
 
Shades are a special case.  If your weapon is made of silver, it behaves
normally.  Otherwise, the base damage for the weapon (Sdam,Ldam) is ZERO,
and the weapon's plus does NOT add (but neither does the rusting penalty).
However, if your weapon is blessed, you still inflict the +d4 damage.  Also,
if your weapon is made of Silver, the silver bonus (+d20) still applies.
Bonuses for STR still seem to apply, as well.  This is why Shades seem to
be so hard to kill.
 
 
In the following table, "Name" is the real name of the weapon.  "Appearance"
is what a character who is not knowledgeable about weapons (Tourists, etc)
would think the weapon was, if this is different from its normal name.  "Wt"
is Weight, "Sdam" is the amount of damage it does against Man-sized-or-smaller creatures, and "Ldam" is the amount it does against Larger-than-man-sized
creatures.
 
Damage is in "dice".  "d6" means a random amount from 1-6, for example.
A weapon that has plus signs or minus signs after its Name carries
an intrinsic bonus or penalty To-Hit, due to its ease of use or quality of
worksmanship.  (+1 per plus, -1 per minus)
 
Avg Dmg is the average amount of damage that a +0 weapon of that type can be
expected to inflict each time it hits.  Keep in mind that the game works off
a random d20 die roll to determine whether or not a weapon hits, so taking a
weapon's intrinsic plus/minus into account is very important.  A weapon that
only averages 5 points of damage, but hits 10% more often might be more
valuable than a weapon that averages 6 points of damage, if you *REALLY* need
to hit that monster.  The amount before the slash is the amount it can be
expected to inflict on a Man-sized-or-smaller creature, and the amount after
the slash is for Larger-than-man-sized creatures.
 
 
